(5894744, 857294, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on a well-deserved blue ribbon.  Great catch.  I''m curious to know if you had this idea in advance or grabbed the moment. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was aiming for something like that but it came out better than I hoped. I really enjoy taking photos of horses where one horse frames another and have taken some photos before like that, see this one for example:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=847812" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1154/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_847812.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1154/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_847812.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1154/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_847812.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Many thanks for the comment Larry.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-08 11:39:12.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by citymars: Congratulations on a well-deserved blue ribbon.  Great catch.  I''m curious to know if you had this idea in advance or grabbed the moment.   I was aiming for something like that but it came out better than I hoped. I really enjoy taking photos of horses where one horse frames another and have taken some photos before like that, see this one for example:  Many thanks for the comment Larry.', '2010-03-08 11:33:19.000000', '2010-03-08 11:39:12.000000', 0),
