(5897013, 857215, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/><b>First impressions</b> are that the model is a little overwhelmed by all the flowers.<br/> <br/><b>Technically</b> this is good. Exposure is good, tones are nice, composition is ok but not one I favour too much.<br/> <br/><b>Artistically</b> I want to like this but find something pulling me back. Her face is made up lovely and her pose is great - sort of a sleeping beauty thing. I find she almost gets lost in the mass of flowers. Perhaps a square crop with less torso would have reduced that effect.<br/> <br/><b>In summary</b> a lovely shot but the flowers detract from the model a little.<br/> <br/>Feel free to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=47541" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PM me</a> if you have any queries.<br/>Gerry</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First impressions are that the model is a little overwhelmed by all the flowers. Technically this is good. Exposure is good, tones are nice, composition is ok but not one I favour too much. Artistically I want to like this but find something pulling me back. Her face is made up lovely and her pose is great - sort of a sleeping beauty thing. I find she almost gets lost in the mass of flowers. Perhaps a square crop with less torso would have reduced that effect. In summary a lovely shot but the flowers detract from the model a little. Feel free to PM me if you have any queries.Gerry', '2010-03-09 17:23:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5897209, 857082, 96572, '<td valign="top">Awesome finish ... congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-03-09 19:12:55.</i></td>', 'Awesome finish ... congrats!', '2010-03-09 19:12:22.000000', '2010-03-09 19:12:55.000000', 0),
(5897520, 857481, 54645, '<td valign="top">Hmm...I liked this Robert. I thought this would  push the potential DNMC crowd. The hand frame is obvious, but the framing by the scene in the background is not. Glad to see you got the Corey comment too, and you got yourself bumped to a 2! LOL!! Well done, I like the background, brings out the craziness of the whole image for me. Scored it well. Cheers.</td>', 'Hmm...I liked this Robert. I thought this would  push the potential DNMC crowd. The hand frame is obvious, but the framing by the scene in the background is not. Glad to see you got the Corey comment too, and you got yourself bumped to a 2! LOL!! Well done, I like the background, brings out the craziness of the whole image for me. Scored it well. Cheers.', '2010-03-09 23:01:54.000000', NULL, 0),
